## Context
Author ruling, 2026-10-27 raid (1249's doifetch half, options B then C). DOIfetch is a separate project
(`MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch` on GitHub, a fork of `hanhan6688/DoiHarvest`), not a script to vendor. Colleagues
asked for it, so it must install in one command. Step B lands in the DOIfetch repo: a console entry point
`doifetch`, open and institutional sources (Crossref, Unpaywall, HAL, ISTEX, EZproxy) as the default
source list, and a README install line (`uv tool install git+https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch`).
The harness neither adds nor enables shadow-library sources; enabling any source outside the default
list stays a manual, per-user choice.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `idh install` installs DOIfetch as a uv tool pinned to a recorded ref (or reports clearly that uv or
      the network is unavailable), idempotently; a test on a temporary HOME with a stubbed `uv`.
- [ ] The zotero skill gains a "fetch missing fulltexts" step that calls `doifetch` with the default
      (open and institutional) source list only, for the works the cited-works check reports missing, and
      says what to do when `doifetch` is absent.
- [ ] Tracker 1249's doifetch child line points here; the harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
adapters/lifecycle.py, bin/idh, skills/zotero/SKILL.md, skills/zotero/references/*, tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py

Related: [[1249]], [[1257]].

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27)
**Premise check.** Holds on DOIfetch (read at 3e074798): `[project.scripts] doifetch = "fetch:main"`; README install line is `uv tool install git+https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch`; no `--source` = Crossref, Unpaywall, HAL, ISTEX, EZproxy (EZproxy skipped without `EZPROXY_BASE`/`EZPROXY_COOKIES`); scihub/libgen only by naming `--source`; flags `--doi`, `--isbn`, `--title`, `--source`, `--no-check-zotero`. Wrinkle: the "cited-works check" is not a harness command. It is a per-project test (`rules/prose-adherence-tests.md:22`, reference `tests/test_cited_works_available.py` in climate-finance-het); the harness-side check that reports works lacking a stored file is `/zotero check-staging` (and `suggest-attachments` files a fetched PDF). The step names the check by its role, not a path.
**Simplest path / antipatterns.** `lifecycle.install_links()` already runs `install_bin(...)` before the receipt write; add one sibling `install_doifetch()` called beside it, nothing else: no manifest entry (not a link), no receipt (uv owns the tool dir), no new config file. Optional-tool precedent: `install_links` skips an optional entry whose target is absent; here a missing `uv` or failed network prints a `report("SKIPPED", ..., repair)` line and returns 0 (optional, so it must not fail the install; the ticket asks "reports clearly", not "fails"). Idempotency: ask `uv tool list` for `doifetch` at the pinned ref and do nothing when it matches; otherwise `uv tool install --force git+https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch@<ref>`. Pin, one place: a module constant `DOIFETCH_REF = "3e074798b0c0bf0b010c444ea701ab8768213294"` (plus URL) in `adapters/lifecycle.py`; the skill text carries no ref. YAGNI: no version-range logic, no uninstall, no `check`/`status` row.
**Actions in order.** (1) Write the failing test. (2) Add the constants and `install_doifetch()`; call it in `install_links` after `install_bin`. (3) Add the zotero step. (4) Point 1249's doifetch child line at this ticket (already the case; confirm it, tick on merge). (5) Gate.
**First failing test** (`tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py`, reuse the `machine` fixture): put a stub `uv` script in the fixture's PATH dir that appends `"$*"` to a log, answers `tool list` from a state file, and makes `tool install` write the state file. Run `idh install` twice. Assert: the log holds one `tool install ... DOIfetch@3e074798...` line after run 1 and none after run 2 (idempotent), exit 0 both times. Second case: no `uv` on PATH, so rc 0, stderr names `uv` and the repair. No network, temp HOME.
**Tautology check.** The test must fail first against HEAD (no `uv tool install` line yet); asserting the ref via the module constant would be circular, so assert the literal 40-hex string in the log and have it equal the one in the ticket log. Existing tests keep passing only if the fixture PATH has no real `uv` (it is `/usr/bin:/bin`; confirm `which uv` is not there, else the stub must shadow it, which it does by being first).
**Zotero step wording (proposed, appended to the verb table notes in `skills/zotero/SKILL.md`, detail in `references/backfill.md`).** "Fetch missing fulltexts. For the works a staging or cited-works check reports without a stored file (`check-staging` verdict `absent` / `has_file: false`), run `doifetch --doi <doi> --title <title>` with no `--source`: the default list is open and institutional only (Crossref, Unpaywall, HAL, ISTEX, EZproxy). Then file each downloaded PDF with `suggest-attachments --parent <itemKey> <file>`, adding `--edit` after inspecting the report. Never pass `--source scihub` or `--source libgen`; enabling any source outside the default list is the author's own manual, per-user choice, never the harness's. When `command -v doifetch` fails, say so and tell the user to run `idh install` (needs `uv` and network); do not fetch another way." Exact verdict names to be matched against `references/backfill.md` at implementation.
**Files.** `adapters/lifecycle.py`, `tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py`, `skills/zotero/SKILL.md`, `skills/zotero/references/backfill.md`; `bin/README` untouched; `make skills-catalog` only if the frontmatter changes (it will not).
**Feasibility.** Confirmed: `install_links`, `install_bin`, `report`, the `machine` fixture, `bin/idh` routing of `install` to `lifecycle.main`. Risk: tests currently pass `PATH` without `uv`; a real `uv` on a dev machine is shadowed by the stub. Exit criteria unchanged. GO.
